## Context
Found incidentally while running `make check` on an unrelated branch
(ticket 0639, 2026-09-04): `bench/check_ticket_logs.py` fails on `origin/main`
as of `a947e71` (the commit that closed and archived 0635):

    FAIL: tickets/closed/0635-tmpdir-xdg-home-redirection-for-zoteus-s.erg:10:
    stamped 2026-09-04T06:10Z, written 2026-09-04T05:40Z
    1 log entry is stamped after the commit that wrote it.

This is pre-existing on `main`, not introduced by this ticket's own work, and
blocks `make check`/`make lint`'s `ticket-logs` target for every branch until
fixed. By the time this raid picked the ticket up, two more commits had
landed and grown the count to 3 (see log entry above) — same defect class,
same check, still a one-line-per-file fix each.

## Relevant files
- `tickets/closed/0635-tmpdir-xdg-home-redirection-for-zoteus-s.erg:10` — drifted stamp, corrected
- `tickets/0613-zoteus-passes-goal-1-i-can-install-it-an.erg:26` — drifted stamp, corrected
- `tickets/closed/0630-gap-b-write-uninstall-md-as-the-r15-remo.erg:15` — drifted stamp, corrected
- `bench/check_ticket_logs.py` — the gate that caught all three

## Actions
1. Find the commit that actually introduced each drifted line
   (`git log -L N,N:path` or equivalent) and read its real timestamp.
2. Correct the stamp on that line to the time the commit evidences, per
   `rules/workflow.md`'s general instruction: "Correct the stamp to a time
   the record evidences … never the other way round."

## Verification
- [x] `python3 bench/check_ticket_logs.py` passes on `main` after the fix

## Exit criteria
- [x] `make check`'s `ticket-logs` target is green on `main`
